{
  "_provenance": {
    "what": "Whether the Stellar EndpointV2/ULN302 contract ids pinned by upstream @layerzerolabs/lz-stellar-sdk@3.0.167 are the ones LayerZero runs today. The ULN302 id is hashed into the DVN attestation, so a superseded id produces a signature aimed at a contract no live verifier reads.",
    "capturedAt": "2026-08-28T08:27:12Z",
    "sources": {
      "pinnedTable": "gasolina-audit/packages/contracts/lz-stellar-sdk/src/contractGetters.ts lines 40-43 (testnet) and 60-63 (mainnet)",
      "liveMetadata": "https://metadata.layerzero-api.com/v1/metadata/deployments",
      "onChain": "https://api.stellar.expert/explorer/{public,testnet}/contract/<id>"
    },
    "howToRegenerate": "Re-run the probe in this repo history: fetch the metadata deployments document, then read each contract id from stellar.expert. No key needed.",
    "verdict": "Two separate generations by the SAME deployer per network, not a metadata error. Generation 1 (pinned) and generation 2 (live) have disjoint wasm hashes for BOTH EndpointV2 and ULN302, and generation 2 was deployed ~3.5 months later. Signing against generation 1 is therefore not trustworthy."
  },
